keywords:
  - encephalitis
  - children
  - WISC-IV
  - intellectual outcome
  - follow-up
  - Vietnam
abstract: >-
  ENCOG is a bilingual (Vietnamese/English) web application that helps clinicians
  and researchers interpret WISC-IV index scores obtained by trained examiners in
  children after encephalitis. It applies the 23-point discrepancy rule to choose a
  representative summary index (FSIQ, GAI or CPI), visualises the four-index profile,
  checks follow-up timing, produces family, school and clinical reports, and
  summarises study cohorts with data checks and charts, including the effect of
  assessment timing and Firth logistic regression for factors associated with a
  summary index below 70. All processing happens in
  the browser; no data are stored or transmitted. ENCOG contains no WISC-IV items
  or norm tables and does not make diagnoses.
